  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Hélène Faggionato served as chair of Le Petit Coeur, a Swiss foundation supporting heart surgery for children in countries with limited medical services. Its volunteer medical teams operate in Mozambique and Cambodia, while the foundation pays for equipment, medicines and other supplies. Working alongside local doctors and nurses, the teams also help them develop the skills to carry out operations themselves.\n\nIn her consular work, Faggionato-Knight supported a Monaco Economic Board mission to Zurich. The programme brought lawyers, bankers and entrepreneurs from the two countries together for business meetings. It also combined commercial discussions with a joint production by the Zurich and Monte-Carlo opera houses.",
    "html": "<p>Hélène Faggionato served as chair of Le Petit Coeur, a Swiss foundation supporting heart surgery for children in countries with limited medical services. Its volunteer medical teams operate in Mozambique and Cambodia, while the foundation pays for equipment, medicines and other supplies. Working alongside local doctors and nurses, the teams also help them develop the skills to carry out operations themselves.</p>\r\n<p>In her consular work, Faggionato-Knight supported a Monaco Economic Board mission to Zurich. The programme brought lawyers, bankers and entrepreneurs from the two countries together for business meetings. It also combined commercial discussions with a joint production by the Zurich and Monte-Carlo opera houses.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 105,
